  "description": "The bare bones of this creamed spinach recipe are pretty straightforward and classic: The spinach is cooked low and slow to gradually concentrate its juices. Combined with a creamy béchamel sauce, it reduces into a rich, thick coating with a near pudding-like texture. The only minor embellishments I include here are a doubling-up of the alliums and a last-minute shot of crème fraîche for a final dose of creaminess and fresh flavor.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 57 g Parmigiano-Reggiano, finely grated (about 1 cup; optional)\n\nNotes: For a homemade version, learn how to make your crème fraîche from scratch.",
